{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1346958-how-would-the-unconquered-sun-respond-to-an-infernal-exalt","id":1346958,"title":"How would the Unconquered Sun respond to an Infernal Exalt?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Infernal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-11-08T01:04:24-08:00","id":1346958,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> How would the Unconquered Sun respond to an Infernal Exalt?","content":"I had this on the backburner, but seeing the 'ask the unconquered sun' thread made me want to write this down. <br /> <br /> Backstory time! <br /> <br /> I was wondering about writing an SI in Creation. Then I realized that most people don't want to see boring old me in Exalted. I wouldn't. But the concept of having foreknowledge and understanding of Exalted from the outer perspective is pretty much irresistible to me. So I had an idea. Why not play the mentor role? So, say, instead of me getting an exaltation, it's someone else. Someone, like, say, an Infernal. Or a Solar. Someone that my 'drop in from real world' character could lend guidance to as someone who already knew what their powers were, how they worked, and what they could do. So that was that. <br /> <br /> The infernal in question: <br /> <br /> A 14 year old girl thief, who was a street urchin. Frightened. Fearful. Timid. Non-confrontational.... so good at avoiding confrontation, that she's pretty much high stealth, high larceny. Capable of going about her business in absolute darkness, and steal from nearly anywhere. Good with tactics and strategy, willing to set fires and sabotage as a distraction. Well, she was goign about her business.... when she got kidnapped by raiders. Slavers. She got free.... and got caught again. This time, they were angry. They beat her. They hamstrung her. And they threw her into the brig to rot, until they got bored. <br /> <br /> In the darkness, crippled, bleeding, and knowing her likely fate, she wept, cursing herself. She should have been faster. She shouldn't have hesitated. She shouldn't have been so careless. She shouldn't have been so afraid. And then, a knock on the door came. A demon entered, bearing an infernal exaltation. And then.... transformation. <br /> <br /> The raiders never knew who it was that poisoned their supplies. But after a few days in the mountains with no food and the crippling pain induced by the poison, it didn't matter anymore. <br /> <br /> And then, the girl wandered away. Her unwoven coadjucator a silent voice in her head, urging her to go claim her destiny and birthright. But Exaltation doesn't change people... at least, not that fast, and her being a favoured of Cecylene and the Ebon Dragon, she wasn't much in the mood for doing anything. At this point, she meets the SI.... who served as a hard anchor for her, and someone who can tell her wtf is going on. <br /> <br /> Here's the thing. Let's say our hypothetical infernal wanders through a celestial gate by accident during Calibration and the Carnival. She wanders the hallways of Yu-shan, wondering at the opulence she's never seen in her years in the back alleys and looking at the gods. She isn't halted.... a combination of ebon dragon charms and a cecylene charm that gives her bonuses against spirits means that the gods around her don't notice her. <br /> <br /> That is... until she bumps into someone big and heavy. She crashes to the floor, and looks up to see a giant, golden four-armed man. And the Unconquered Sun looks at her, and realizing something is wrong, decides to <i>focus</i>. And at this point, her disguise is torn apart by the sheer might of Sol Invictus's personal attention, and she meets him face to face, Infernal Exalt meeting the Unconquered Sun for the first time. <br /> <br /> What can be the potential fallout and consequences for this first meeting?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-08T01:22:37-08:00","id":1346960,"title":"","content":"Well depending on how cool an awesome the Infernal was maybe the Unconquered Sun would go, &quot;Oh holy shit, I can't believe I just bumped into <i>you</i> here of all places! Seriously, I'm a <i>huge</i> fan! Look, I don't want to come off as rude or anything, but could I bother you for your autograph? Maybe even a selfie? Seriously, you're the best. I can't wait to see the look on Luna's face when I tell her about this!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-08T01:56:02-08:00","id":1346961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1346958-how-would-the-unconquered-sun-respond-to-an-infernal-exalt?p=1346960#post1346960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well depending on how cool an awesome the Infernal was maybe the Unconquered Sun would go, &amp;quot;Oh holy shit, I can't believe I just bumped into <i>you</i> here of all places! Seriously, I'm a <i>huge</i> fan! Look, I don't want to come off as rude or anything, but could I bother you for your autograph? Maybe even a selfie? Seriously, you're the best. I can't wait to see the look on Luna's face when I tell her about this!&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, she's only been out for a few months. She hasn't done anything world shaking yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-08T03:10:51-08:00","id":1346965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1346958-how-would-the-unconquered-sun-respond-to-an-infernal-exalt#post1346958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tragic Backstory, anime crash into hello</div> </div> </div> </div>Sun Daddy does not give a single solitary fuck. Sorry. He barely takes more than a second when his own God Kings achieve their Exaltation, literally only Zenith are guarenteed an epiphany and that's a flash in the pan. There's not even a full minute of him turning his face toward creation in the last xty hundred years. The guy is a super coke fiend ultra billonaire 80s power executive who is also the world mma champ president of harvard currently playing the Mega Soul Game and screwing the Moon. <br /> <br /> Your character is a waitress who broke a glass. I'd be surprised if he even broke step acknowledging you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-08T04:16:17-08:00","id":1346976,"title":"","content":"Huh. That's unfortunate. I at least would imagine him wondering 'is that a solar exaltation, and why is there the taint of Malfeas and the ebon dragon on it?'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-08T04:48:10-08:00","id":1346982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1346958-how-would-the-unconquered-sun-respond-to-an-infernal-exalt?p=1346965#post1346965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your character is a waitress who broke a glass. I'd be surprised if he even broke step acknowledging you.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think he's the sort who'd tip the waitress having a bad day with an anecdote about how he once had a job waiting tables and just look at where he is now. Their interaction is of course all about him and aleviating his own doubts about himself and the system. However he's kind of oblivious to the fact that by doing so he's drawing attention to the fact she's broken a glass in front of an extremely influential customer and potentially put her job at risk.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-08T05:38:29-08:00","id":1346986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1346958-how-would-the-unconquered-sun-respond-to-an-infernal-exalt?p=1346965#post1346965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sun Daddy does not give a single solitary fuck. Sorry. He barely takes more than a second when his own God Kings achieve their Exaltation, literally only Zenith are guarenteed an epiphany and that's a flash in the pan. There's not even a full minute of him turning his face toward creation in the last xty hundred years. The guy is a super coke fiend ultra billonaire 80s power executive who is also the world mma champ president of harvard currently playing the Mega Soul Game and screwing the Moon.</div> </div> </div> </div>My God... it's fifteen years ago... My time machine worked!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-08T05:47:27-08:00","id":1346990,"title":"","content":"For the general question, I'd be inclined to portray the Unconquered Sun as generally reasonable but with a few things that he can be kind of reactionary about. The Underworld and Yozis are one of those things, theft and transgression upon his Exaltations are another. I would portray a first impression of an Infernal Exalt as being, let's say, in line with what the Yozis intend it to be seen as; an insult and a challenge.<br /> <br /> Albeit one that is ideally addressed by way of the Solar Exalted that it is intended to refute.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-08T06:49:16-08:00","id":1347000,"title":"","content":"The Unconquered Sun id really the best of people that we can imagine, at least at his core he is. That he is broken-hearted and stuck playing the games to avoid facing the world doesn't really change that. In the case of this Infernal suddenly showing up in his presence he would be compelled by his very nature to act. In this case his action would almost certainly be his compassion shining through. He would give her some truly uplifting words and then probably summon Lytek and maybe some other gods of healing to address the afflicting that is the infernal corruption of her exaltation, he is still the king of heaven and there are other gods much better suited to healing this girl. Many other gods may demand some form of punishment or vengeance against the infernal but the Unconquered Sun has absolutely no reason to be anything but compassionate in this situation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-08T06:55:13-08:00","id":1347005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1346958-how-would-the-unconquered-sun-respond-to-an-infernal-exalt?p=1347000#post1347000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Unconquered Sun id really the best of people that we can imagine, at least at his core he is. That he is broken-hearted and stuck playing the games to avoid facing the world doesn't really change that. In the case of this Infernal suddenly showing up in his presence he would be compelled by his very nature to act. In this case his action would almost certainly be his compassion shining through. He would give her some truly uplifting words and then probably summon Lytek and maybe some other gods of healing to address the afflicting that is the infernal corruption of her exaltation, he is still the king of heaven and there are other gods much better suited to healing this girl. Many other gods may demand some form of punishment or vengeance against the infernal but the Unconquered Sun has absolutely no reason to be anything but compassionate in this situation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think your interpretation is the only valid one, I would totally see a more &quot;rigid&quot; Unconquered Sun being in theme. But I like yours more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-08T07:10:22-08:00","id":1347011,"title":"","content":"Maybe he would burn away the Infernal taint and transform her into a real Solar Exalted. But he's also really busy playing the Games of Divinity and intriguing/flirting with the other Incarnae, so he might not even notice her unless she was REALLY beautiful or interesting enough in some other way to catch his attention (other than being an Infernal).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-08T07:27:14-08:00","id":1347016,"title":"","content":"Regardless of how nice or not he is, surely he'll be confused and shocked, and want to know what in Creation this girl is; what's happened to the Solar Exaltation he made? Why is it tainted by the Yozis?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-08T09:12:56-08:00","id":1347045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1346958-how-would-the-unconquered-sun-respond-to-an-infernal-exalt?p=1346986#post1346986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My God... it's fifteen years ago... My time machine worked!</div> </div> </div> </div>Settle down, Doc, it's just a repost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-08T09:36:38-08:00","id":1347051,"title":"","content":"Third Edition is specifically intended to avoid giving any official stance on exactly what kind of person the Sun is, what he\u2019s doing, or how much he\u2019s paying attention.<br /> <br /> He is whatever your storyteller wants him to be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-08T12:48:55-08:00","id":1347084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1346958-how-would-the-unconquered-sun-respond-to-an-infernal-exalt?p=1347045#post1347045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Settle down, Doc, it's just a repost.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can assure you that it is not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-08T16:08:55-08:00","id":1347121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1346958-how-would-the-unconquered-sun-respond-to-an-infernal-exalt?p=1347051#post1347051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Third Edition is specifically intended to avoid giving any official stance on exactly what kind of person the Sun is, what he\u2019s doing, or how much he\u2019s paying attention.<br /> <br /> He is whatever your storyteller wants him to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>now that I've had a coffee and woke up, I'm going to elaborate on my post about the UCS not giving a shit. <br /> <br /> First, What is the Unconquered Sun? He is perfection. He is the ultimate example of anything that anyone could do, and he can it it flawlessly. That is what the core of his essence is: perfection. So the UCS is born-made and the Primordial War happens and yadda yadda yadda, Solars, Usurpation, Jade Prison, let's go. <br /> <br /> The old lore is that the Solars grew vain/bad/hedonistic enough that he Sol Invictus turned his face away from them in disgust or what have you, and just stopped giving a shit about Creation. He is the unequivocal King of the Heavens by right of his being better than everybody at everything (yeah, there's some poilitics and Maidens but whatever. UCS is the Head Honcho). <br /> <br /> So the Jade Prison sat around for a millenia and UCS didn't give a shit. The Solars are back and he does not give a shit. and here's where my basic premise comes in: <b>The Unconquered Sun CANNOT give a shit or there would be no story</b>. <br /> <br /> Sol Invictus used to have stats (which, lets face it, was a bad idea). He could have easily,<b> easily</b>, whupped FaFL and MoW in a single day, but he didn't. There's a problem with having a God that is both <b>Benevolent</b> and <b>Capable- </b>it immediately raises the question of <i><b>why doesnt he just solve the problem himself?</b></i>. I'm not going to touch on real world religions and myths because its a derailing quagmire, but basically: there's a reason the gods are always unable to do stuff or too petty to do stuff. Hell, you can google &quot;the problem of evil&quot; and read a literal <b>library</b> of apologia about this subject. If the UCS cared about the world, he would have fixed everything. He's not the God Emperor of Mankind from Warhammer, who is tied down to a throne (and sorta dead). He's not the gods of DnD, who are bound by laws to not interfere because there's too much opposition on every side. So, <b>the story depends on him not caring. </b>There's literally nothing preventing him from coming down here. <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12952\" data-vbnamecard=\"12952\">Accelerator</a> 's post depends on the assumption that the Unconquered Sun, basically the King of Heaven, does not know about the Infernals and wonders what his reaction would be to finding one. Is there no one in Heaven, no member of the Celestial Bureaucracy, no God, no spirit, no one at all, who has noticed an Infernal in the last 5 years and told him about it? Not one single servant or messenger? No Lunar has ever seen one and told Luna herself? He never once looked down at his Chosen and noticed half of them have been warped or twisted? Ridiculous. Preposterous. Inconceivable. <br /> <br /> The only way the whole shebang works is if the Unconquered Sun simply doesn't give a shit about the Solars or Creation or anything, either because he's callous or he's too wrapped up in the Games of Divinity. There's nothing else stopping him from jumping down and killing each Deathlord one by one otherwise. <br /> <br /> It's up to the Storyteller to invent a reason why. <br /> <br /> <br /> Just for fun, here's a minor and slapdash things he didn't get off his glorious golden ass about<b></b>:<br /> Balorian Crusade<br /> Contagion <br /> Usurpation<br /> Jade Prison<br /> Death Lords<br /> Abyssals<br /> Infernals<br /> Breaking of the Mask<br /> Wyld Hunt<br /> Scarlet Empress<br /> <br /> Now probably someone is gonna jump on this list and explain why, no really he did something on one of those or couldnt because xyz, but piece by piece it spells out what spent too much time talking about. <br /> <br /> The Unconquered Sun doesn't care about any of us.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-08T17:35:27-08:00","id":1347141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">There's literally nothing preventing him from coming down here. [\u2026] The Unconquered Sun doesn't care about any of us.</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> Are you writing a piece from the fallible perspective of one of the fictional characters who inhabits the setting?<br /> <br /> </span></span></span></div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">So the Jade Prison sat around for a millenia and UCS didn't give a shit. The Solars are back and he does not give a shit.</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">\u200bAlternatively, the return of the Solars is itself the representation and mechanism of the Unconquered Sun's attention returning to Creation.<br /> <br /> </span></span></span></div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Sol Invictus used to have stats (which, lets face it, was a bad idea). He could have easily,<b> easily</b>, whupped FaFL and MoW in a single day, but he didn't. There's a problem with having a God that is both <b>Benevolent</b> and <b>Capable- </b>it immediately raises the question of <i><b>why doesnt he just solve the problem himself?</b></i>. I'm not going to touch on real world religions and myths because its a derailing quagmire, but basically: there's a reason the gods are always unable to do stuff or too petty to do stuff. Hell, you can google &quot;the problem of evil&quot; and read a literal <b>library</b> of apologia about this subject. If the UCS cared about the world, he would have fixed everything. He's not the God Emperor of Mankind from Warhammer, who is tied down to a throne (and sorta dead). He's not the gods of DnD, who are bound by laws to not interfere because there's too much opposition on every side. So, <b>the story depends on him not caring. </b>There's literally nothing preventing him from coming down here.</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> Among the stats in Second Edition was the expression of a very severe addiction to the Games of Divinity and extremely high Virtues that would enforce principles of leaving Creation in the hands of the Exalted.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12952\" data-vbnamecard=\"12952\">Accelerator</a> 's post depends on the assumption that the Unconquered Sun, basically the King of Heaven, does not know about the Infernals and wonders what his reaction would be to finding one. Is there no one in Heaven, no member of the Celestial Bureaucracy, no God, no spirit, no one at all, who has noticed an Infernal in the last 5 years and told him about it? Not one single servant or messenger?</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> The Infernal Exalted are being presented in Third Edition as still being a rumour and a mystery. The Sidereals are supposed to be aware of that, but details remain scant.<br /> <br /> That and, yeah, it would be consistent with the characterisation of Yu-Shan, regardless of how one imagines the disposition of the Unconquered Sun, that he's not exactly getting regular reports on things, and certainly plausible that any given figure who does know isn't exactly in a position to convey it. It's reasonable enough that it's not the information that some random servant or messenger would know, or if they did, would have access to the guy.<br /> <br /> I can't recall precisely what Accelerator said in that first post, but there are also ways to approach the narrative that are less binary. Like the idea that the Sun might have been informed ahead of time that they exist in the abstract, but that's not really enough to prepare him for the experience of witnessing one in person. I'd be inclined to portray that as the Unconquered Sun seeing things that run more deeply in a corrupted Solar Essence that no other being can see; things that shock and disturb him.<br /> <br /> </span></span></span></div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">No Lunar has ever seen one and told Luna herself?</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> Infernals are also referred to as a still largely unknown quantity to the Lunar Exalted, and if any random Lunar should happen to learn more they don't exactly have a direct hotline to their non-gender specific patron deity.<br /> <br /> The point about the absence of about half of the Solars presumably being a thing more noticeable to the Sun is a more fair point, though. But again, there could be a difference between knowing that they're gone and knowing exactly what has happened to them, and between that knowledge and the full appreciation of witnessing. </span></span></span></div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The only way the whole shebang works is if the Unconquered Sun simply doesn't give a shit about the Solars or Creation or anything, either because he's callous or he's too wrapped up in the Games of Divinity. There's nothing else stopping him from jumping down and killing each Deathlord one by one otherwise.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">It's up to the Storyteller to invent a reason why.</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> Fair enough for your settling upon your own reason, but it need not be the only one.<br /> <br /> And even in cases where it is a shared reason, it won't always be felt so... emphatically.<br /> <br /> Still, there's the Law of Diminishment to consider; the core book portrays Heaven as rife with rumour that the Incarnae put a lot of the strength they might have once had to face off against greater terrors into their Chosen. <br /> <br /> As powers go, I think it's also worth noting that Accelerator's premise is one with a lot of drama to it, that might be worth playing fast and loose a bit on any powers presumed or implied to be in his possession to bring about.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just for fun, here's a minor and slapdash things he didn't get off his glorious golden ass about<b></b>:</div> </div> </div> </div></span></span></span></div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Balorian Crusade</span></span></span></div><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Contagion</span></span></span></div><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Usurpation</span></span></span></div><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Jade Prison</span></span></span></div><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Death Lords</span></span></span></div><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Abyssals</span></span></span></div><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Infernals</span></span></span></div><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Breaking of the Mask</span></span></span></div><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Wyld Hunt</span></span></span></div><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Scarlet Empress</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> Well, the Usurpation and Jade Prison are already covered under the premise of him turning his face away, and the Wyld Hunt and Scarlet Empress... why would they be presumed to be subjects he intervenes in in the first place?<br /> <br /> I've never gotten the impression that the breaking of the Mask matters to anybody not concerned with astrology.</span></span></span></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-08T18:24:56-08:00","id":1347152,"title":"","content":"Well... Maybe he's decided to leave everything to the solars, and to a being who's been living through the time of glory, the age of sorrows ain't that bad by comparisom?<br /> <br /> Maybe he swore to leave creation to the Exalted, and is keeping to it?<br /> <br /> Maybe he'll have an actual reaction to finding a solar exaltation with ebon dragon and malfean Essence.<br /> <br /> Maybe he's not been told. He's addicted to the games and generally heaven is corrupt, remember?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-08T23:09:54-08:00","id":1347173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1346958-how-would-the-unconquered-sun-respond-to-an-infernal-exalt?p=1346986#post1346986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My God... it's fifteen years ago... My time machine worked!</div> </div> </div> </div>Just found this. You mean that he's going back to the old exalted style of discussion, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-09T01:36:34-08:00","id":1347194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1346958-how-would-the-unconquered-sun-respond-to-an-infernal-exalt?p=1347051#post1347051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Third Edition is specifically intended to avoid giving any official stance on exactly what kind of person the Sun is, what he\u2019s doing, or how much he\u2019s paying attention.<br /> <br /> He is whatever your storyteller wants him to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>In my game he was dead. And had been for years. Splat.<br /> <br /> Not a fan of how the game wrote him.<br /> <br /> I'm also not a huge fan of how 3rd edition writes him, but at least there's less for me to be annoyed by.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-09T06:53:18-08:00","id":1347231,"title":"","content":"2005 Sun (15 years ago, late 1e) probably reacts like Zeus or Odin who looks more Apollo - a canny, calculating god, who is &quot;The Best&quot; and holds pride of place because he is calculating in the use of power, with a fair bit of hubristic pride, lust, sentimentality and other human flaws and virtues which can be his undoing and make him more admirable and human than he seems. Though 2005 people may question what he is doing outside of the Jade Pleasure Dome, and counsel you on the problems of potentially bringing the Sun into your game as an NPC that can squash many challenges. He's not any sort of perfectly morally wise figure, and probably reacts in a fair bit of a way that is shaped by a calculation of how he can use her, but also by some sentiment. Not predictable.<br /> <br /> 2010 Sun (10 years ago, very late 2e) is probably Aslan meets Jesus meets Superman and acts much like you'd expect that to.<br /> <br /> I don't know about 2019-2020 Sun, but probably less like Jesus-Superman-Aslan by removing the idea of him being a god of limitless compassion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-21T13:26:40-08:00","id":1350101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1346958-how-would-the-unconquered-sun-respond-to-an-infernal-exalt#post1346958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What can be the potential fallout and consequences for this first meeting?</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess the many questions are, what sort of Unconquered Sun are you needing for your story? What do you want your Infernal to get out of it? What do you want her to learn?<br /> <br /> You're writing the story. So the Unconquered Sun can be as addicted to the Games as you need him to be.<br /> <br /> So define first what your Infernal will come away with from the meeting, and extrapolate from there. What do you want her to accomplish?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3012,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3012-uknown-darklord","user":"Uknown DarkLord","date":". 11-22-2019, 08:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3012-uknown-darklord","name":"Uknown DarkLord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3012_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-22T07:58:19-08:00","id":1350235,"title":"","content":"Honestly, with how The Unconquered Sun can see intimacies and all in the Glories write up, he may just call Lytek over and tell him to find out what is going on with the infernal exaltation and depart from there. He's done his job, and got the ball rolling. <br /> <br /> From there, it is up to the Infernal to cultivate a relationship with Lytek and possibly the Gold Faction. <br /> <br /> But again, that depends on the story you are trying to tell. It is equally plausible that Ignis Divine just says, &quot;excuse me&quot;, and ignores her. Or maybe he sees this as an opportunity to flip an agent of Hell and says something inspiring.<br /> <br /> But again. the main question is, what do you want your infernal to get out of it? What sort of story do you want it to be. That will determine how TUS responds more than anything else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3012-uknown-darklord","name":"Uknown DarkLord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3012_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-28T18:49:41-08:00","id":1351567,"title":"","content":"I believe Ink Monkeys sort of answered this in 2e on the subject of how Nysela would react to Infernals in the context of offering them a chance to pilot the Daystar: She would be strictly meritocratic, asking them what they are willing to offer in defense of Creation, and judge them by their actions not their nature. Given that Nysela largely takes her lead from the Sun and the Sun having been the most Virtuous thing in Creation prior to his seclusion I think this could be a fairly good model. Except of course, as others have said, maybe with the Sun being a lot more jaded and world-wearied than he once was. Still that Intimacy of cautious optimism's got to count for something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12360-guitar-longcat","name":"Guitar Longcat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-29T01:24:43-08:00","id":1351614,"title":"","content":"If I were running that story I'd have the Unconquered Sun take a good, hard look at the new Infernal and imprint a vision in her head &quot;Never forget that you are one of mine. Prove yourself worthy.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800080\">I express my opinions, but YSMV; Your Stories May Vary.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\"><i>Formerly known as wyrmpuff</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12288-mal-akh","name":"Mal'akh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12288_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-02T01:28:02-08:00","id":1352123,"title":"","content":"My feeling has always been that his reaction to Infernal Exalted would be to laugh at the foolishness of the Yozis, who put in all the work to research and corrupt Exaltations and yet still clearly don't understand what Exaltation <i>is</i>, how it really works, or why it defeated them.<br /> <br /> Exaltation is a way for gods (and others) to bestow their powers on mortals. It isn't a tool or a weapon. It's not, in and of itself, a way to make loyal soldiers or armies. When the UCS first sent his Exaltations out into the world, he was placing profound trust in humanity. That trust has sometimes been betrayed or shaken, but it's still the cornerstone of how Exaltation works. The Creation-Ruling Mandate was just a formal statement of a reality that the Incarnae had irrevocably established the moment they sent their Exalted into the world - the reality that the world now belonged to humanity, not to the gods.<br /> <br /> Whatever they may have thought, the Yozis, in creating the Infernal Exalted, were not challenging or threatening the Creation-Ruling Mandate (let alone the Celestial Incarnae, who are largely retired in any case.) They were <i>endorsing</i> it - signing their names to it, irrevocably granting their power and glory to the very humans and Exalted who defeated them, in a surrender more absolute and final than the end of the Primordial War itself. Unlike the Yozis, the Unconquered Sun understands that it is the human heart behind an Exaltation that makes the actual decisions and that decides what that Exaltation actually means. They're not going to change that just by painting the Chosen green and granting them Infernal magic.<br /> <br /> That doesn't mean he wouldn't be concerned too, of course - Infernal Exalted are still dangerous, especially if they listen to demons whispering in their ears when they shouldn't (a problem all the Exalted have had in the past.) But ultimately he's going to know at a glance that this won't go the way the Yozis want it to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 12-02-2019, 02:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-02T13:52:33-08:00","id":1352213,"title":"","content":"Probably (2e's) Ebon Dragon right now:<br /> <br /> &quot;Ah yes, heavy is the head that <i>doesn't</i> wear the crown and then lives in eternal luxury in the Pleasure Dome (such humility, merely the supreme generalissimo-for-immortal-life of a vast divine bureaucracy that reaches into every facet of Creation! only the loved and object of every god's envy, bestriding the Games as the star athlete on an eternal victory lap!), then at some point withdraws one's favour from their Chosen following which they were *totally coincidentally* betrayed and banished to the Jade Prison, for all eternity, until *I* played my hand... But really, great stuff Sun, just marvellous stuff. Totally gonna steal that for when I'm standing behind the throne in Heaven and the Infernals rule humanity as their overlords!&quot;.<br /> <br /> (In which I impersonate a &quot;Yozi Apologist&quot; that deliberately puts the worse spin on this. Not that I don't buy Aquillion's post at least a little, but there's always an answer back, in Exalted!)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}